# sapintegrationsuite_number_range (Resource)

A number range hands out unique, increasing numbers, typically interchange control numbers for
outbound EDIFACT or X12 documents. It has two kinds of data: the static configuration (range,
rotation, padding), which Terraform manages like any other attribute, and the live counter,
which deployed content advances with every message. The resource separates the two so that an
ordinary apply never resets a counter that is in use.

**Status:** supported. Backed by `NumberRanges` of the Message Stores API. SAP documents only
create and update. Reading by name, delete and import work on a tenant but are not documented,
so they need `enable_unofficial = true`.

## Prerequisites

- An OAuth client with `MonitoringArtifactsDeploy`.
- Terraform 1.11 or later, because `current_value_wo` is write-only.

## Lifecycle

With `enable_unofficial = true`:

| Operation | What happens |
|---|---|
| Create | Stops if a number range of that name exists (SAP does not document what a create over it does), then creates it with the counter from `current_value_wo`. |
| Read | Reads the static fields and the live counter into `current_value`. Changes made in the UI show as drift; a number range deleted outside Terraform drops out of state. |
| Update | Sends the static fields. The counter is sent from `current_value_wo` only when `current_value_wo_version` changed; otherwise the provider reads the live counter right before the `PUT` and sends it back, because SAP rejects an update without one. |
| Replacement | Changing `name` deletes the number range and creates a new one. |
| Delete | Deletes the number range. Content that still uses it fails at runtime afterwards. |

Without the switch, only the documented create and update run:

| Operation | What happens |
|---|---|
| Create | Creates the number range without checking whether the name exists. `current_value` is the counter that was sent; `deployed_by` and `deployed_on` stay empty. |
| Read | Keeps the state as it is. Drift is not detected. |
| Update | Only allowed together with a new `current_value_wo_version`, which sets the counter to `current_value_wo`. A plan that changes only the static fields fails, because keeping the live counter would require reading it. |
| Replacement, delete | Refused at plan time. Use `terraform state rm` to stop managing a number range. |

**Setting the counter deliberately.** Change `current_value_wo_version` (for example to a date)
together with `current_value_wo`. That is the only way the configured counter reaches SAP after
the number range exists.

